+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number) and answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` for the tickets it
+  imported (`dishes` is the number of dishes sold). Tickets already imported
+  are skipped. A bad row (`bad_request`) or an item running out
+  (`sale_not_enough_stock`) imports nothing; the message names the row,
+  `row 2` being the first data row.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists per item
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }` for the days
+  from `from` to `to` inclusive, for items where either use is above zero.
